  "final_message": "Fixed. The root cause was in `collect` in `billing/payments.py`. When a customer had no default payment method, it returned `None` straight away. It never called `record_failure`, so nothing counted the attempt, scheduled a retry, emitted `invoice.payment_failed`, or moved the subscription to `past_due`.\n\nIt now calls `record_failure(ctx, invoice, \"no_payment_method\")` before returning, the same way the expired-card path already does. The existing 24 tests pass. I didn't add a test for the no-payment-method case.\n\nI also wrote `answer.json` with `{\"file\": \"payments.py\", \"function\": \"collect\"}`.",
